From 13d0e78269efe70a8155c2121b1aa7326a79377d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Christian=20K=C3=BCndig?= <christian@kuendig.info>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:26:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] nvapi: Add undocumented CUDA topology entry point
 0x36e39e6b

Legacy PhysX looks up the undocumented entry point 0x36e39e6b (see
issue #313) next to CudaEnumComputeCapableGpus. PhysXDevice 18.12.7.2
uses it to select the PhysX GPU and its CUDA ordinal, and passes a V2
topology followed by three zero arguments. Name it
NvAPI_CUDA_EnumComputeCapableByTopology and return the same array as
CudaEnumComputeCapableGpus V2 for GPUs confirmed by CUDA, without
checking or changing the version. Use a variadic cdecl signature that
only reads the first argument. Return NVAPI_NO_IMPLEMENTATION when CUDA
did not confirm any GPU.

Keep such entry points in a separate table, include it in
DXVK_NVAPI_DISABLE_ENTRYPOINTS and in validate-methods.py. 0xd875b6c5,
which is called differently, stays unknown.

Link the real nvapi_QueryInterface into the tests and check lookups,
including disabled entry points in separate processes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
